# Long-Term Memory Protocol (via Obsidian MCP)

## 1. Initialization (Read Phase)
At the start of a new session or complex task, DO NOT guess or hallucinate past context.
- Use `search_vault` to find relevant documentation.
- Example: for the AI agents marketers platform, search "AI agents marketers platform architecture" or relevant tags.
- For automation work, search for existing n8n workflows or WordPress/WooCommerce integration notes.
- Read relevant notes with `read_note` before proposing code changes.

## 2. Active Development (Execution Phase)
- Rely on extracted memory to guide code generation.
- On recurring errors or package conflicts, search the vault for prior solutions.

## 3. Reflection and Archiving (Write Phase)
On major milestones, complex bug fixes, or architectural decisions — document automatically:
- Create or update a note summarizing the outcome.
- Update corresponding `.md` files in Obsidian when finalizing content plans or structures.
- Save prompt structures and finalized concepts in the appropriate Obsidian folder.
- Format new notes with YAML frontmatter and relevant tags (`#ai`, `#architecture`, `#n8n`, `#marketing`).
- Use `[[wiki-links]]` to connect new notes to existing concepts from the Read Phase.

Always inform the user briefly when reading from or writing to Obsidian.
